hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-15 = cons "*Science* is from *scire*, to know, whose deeper root means to cut, to split: *schism*, *schizo-*, *shed*, and in some accounts *conscious*. Knowing as cutting. *Consciousness*, *con* + *scire*, is knowing-together. So the word for consciousness says knowing with: a cut made with someone. You can cut alone and get science; you cut together and get consciousness. Interpersonal computing is, in the words, conscious computing." (cons "" nil)
